# Whitelist: package only what VS Code needs at runtime.
# Everything else (src/, build.mjs, scripts/, exemplos/, .github/, screenshots, CONTRIBUTING.md...) stays out.
# The lines match only the names the build generates. A stray file with such a name (themes/serena-*-color-theme.json,
# or an .svg directly inside icons/dark, light, hc or icons/logos/<mode>) would still be packaged: "node build.mjs"
# deletes it and "node scripts/check.mjs" fails on it, so run both before packaging by hand.
# A new variant whose id does not start with "serena-", or a new icon theme, needs its own line
# (node scripts/check.mjs says so).
**
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!images/icon.png
!themes/serena-*-color-theme.json
!icons/serena-icons.json
!icons/serena-icons-minimal.json
!icons/dark/*.svg
!icons/light/*.svg
!icons/logos/dark/*.svg
!icons/logos/light/*.svg
!icons/hc/*.svg
!icons/logos/hc/*.svg
